.TH SPOTLIT 1 "Spotlit" "Spotlit Manual"
.SH NAME
spotlit \- manage Bing and Windows Spotlight wallpapers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spotlit
.RI [ --background ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Spotlit
maintains a local wallpaper library and applies wallpapers manually or on a
configurable schedule. On Linux, it retrieves recent Bing wallpapers. On
Windows, it uses Windows Spotlight metadata when available.
.PP
Starting Spotlit does not change the desktop wallpaper, install the optional
GNOME Shell extension, or modify extension preferences. Those actions require
explicit interaction in the application.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --background
Start without presenting the main window. This mode is used by startup
integration and keeps Spotlit available through its system tray icon.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/spotlit
Per-user configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/spotlit
Per-user application data on Linux.
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://github.com/oksyd/spotlit
Project website
.UE
